<title>USA: TABLE - KEPCO sells $200 mln bonds.</title>
<headline>TABLE - KEPCO sells $200 mln bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Korea Electric Power Corp (KEPCO) was priced on Wednesday, according to lead manager Lehman Brother.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale will be used for general corporate purposes including capital expenditures, debt-refinancing and overseas investments.</p>
<p>BORROWER KOREA ELECTRIC POWER CORP</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 6.75 PCT   MATURITY 8/1/2027</p>
<p>TYPE BONDS	   ISS PRICE 99.672  FIRST PAY DATE 2/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A1    YIELD 6.81 PCT    PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P AA-MINUS  SPREAD +77 BPS    PUTABLE IN THE SEVENTH</p>
<p>								    YEAR</p>
<p>((Caryn Trokie, 212-859-1678))</p>
